## Key Design Decisions

1. **No Database Required** — All state is in-memory per session. This keeps the prototype fast and dependency-free. Sessions persist until server restart.

2. **Gemini as the LLM** — All agents use the same Gemini API key with different system prompts. The "multi-agent" behavior is achieved through prompt engineering + structured output parsing.

3. **Supervisor Pattern** — The Supervisor agent uses JSON-mode output to classify intent and route to workers. Workers return structured updates that merge into the shared state.

4. **No External APIs (Simulated)** — Since Google Places, Maps, etc. require separate API keys and billing, the Scout and Orchestrator agents will use their LLM knowledge to provide realistic venue/vendor recommendations. The architecture is designed so real API tools can be plugged in later.

